From 6560236480391492e19c3110e0bfbdbe0ac09825 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 19:09:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lane-298: drain the compute queue before a host-path kv-zero
 memset (host-visible UMA buffers)

HQ86 18:42: the CPU memset branch of ggml_vk_buffer_memset (host-visible UMA
buffers) has the same race as the GPU path closed in 00209ea977: graph
compute returns without a wait, so a CPU zero can land before an in-flight
graph K write. Wait for the compute queue to go idle (queue handle lock +
vkQueueWaitIdle) under the device mutex before the CPU write. waitIdle, not
a fence submit: ggml_vk_queue_command_pools_cleanup would reset an open
memset batch's command buffer on the same pool.

Served config: 0 host fills on every kvzs load (cells/kvzs-10091800), so no
served cost expected; correctness on every path.

Origin: lane-298
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED (gated by the kvzo cell: ids vs v0.1.3.1 + served ABBA; host path has 0 exposure there)
---
 ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-buffers.cpp | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-buffers.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-buffers.cpp
index 67790ecdb4..b369d77cfd 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-buffers.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-buffers.cpp
@@ -1697,6 +1697,13 @@ void ggml_vk_buffer_memset(vk_buffer& dst, size_t offset, uint32_t c, size_t siz
 
     if (dst->memory_property_flags & vk::MemoryPropertyFlagBits::eHostVisible &&
         dst->device->uma) {
+        // lane-298 (HQ86 18:42): same race as the GPU path; drain the compute queue so no in-flight graph write lands
+        // after the CPU zero. waitIdle, not a fence submit: a pool cleanup here would reset an open batch's buffer.
+        std::lock_guard<std::recursive_mutex> guard(dst->device->mutex);
+        vk_queue_handle & q = *dst->device->compute_queue->handle;
+        q.lock();
+        q.queue.waitIdle();
+        q.unlock();
         memset((uint8_t*)dst->ptr + offset, c, size);
         return;
     }
